# modules/sast/rules/go.rules - docs/DESIGN.md §6.3 "go" seed catalog:
# exec.Command with concatenation, text/template used for HTML output,
# math/rand for secrets, SQL string concatenation, InsecureSkipVerify:true.
#
# Path note: docs/DESIGN.md §3's tree lists this pack simply as "go.rules"
# alongside its siblings (secrets.rules, crypto.rules, injection.rules,
# python.rules), all of which live under modules/sast/rules/ per
# rules/RULE-FORMAT.md §9's frozen path table
# (`modules/sast/rules/*.rules`). A bare modules/sast/go.rules would match
# no row of that table and fail E070, so this file is shipped here, one
# directory level below the shorthand the ticket used.

id: SAST-GO-EXEC_CONCAT-01
title: exec.Command built from a concatenated string
severity: critical
confidence: medium
cwe: CWE-78
owasp: A03:2021
pattern: exec\.Command\([^)]*\+
dialect: ere
files: *.go
tags: static
tags: quick
remediation: Pass each argument to exec.Command as its own slice element instead of
  concatenating untrusted input into a command or argument string, and never route a
  concatenated string through a shell (`"sh", "-c", ...`). If a shell is unavoidable,
  validate or escape every concatenated component first.
references: CWE-78

id: SAST-GO-TEMPLATE_HTML-01
title: text/template used where html/template is required
severity: high
confidence: medium
cwe: CWE-79
owasp: A03:2021
pattern: "text/template"
dialect: ere
files: *.go
context-require: ResponseWriter
context-window: 15
tags: static
remediation: Use html/template, not text/template, whenever the rendered output is HTML
  written to an http.ResponseWriter. text/template performs no contextual auto-escaping,
  so any request-derived value reaching the template is a reflected XSS sink.
references: CWE-79

id: SAST-GO-WEAK_RANDOM-01
title: math/rand used to generate a token, session id, or secret
severity: high
confidence: medium
cwe: CWE-338
owasp: A02:2021
pattern: "math/rand"
dialect: ere
files: *.go
context-require: (token|Token|session|Session|password|Password|secret|Secret|auth|Auth)
context-window: 15
tags: static
remediation: Use crypto/rand, not math/rand, for anything used as a token, session id, or
  secret. math/rand is a deterministic PRNG seeded from a small state space and is
  predictable to an attacker who observes even a little output.
references: CWE-338

id: SAST-GO-SQL_CONCAT-01
title: SQL statement built by string concatenation or Sprintf formatting
severity: critical
confidence: medium
cwe: CWE-89
owasp: A03:2021
pattern: (["'](SELECT|INSERT|UPDATE|DELETE)[^"']*["'][[:space:]]*\+|fmt\.Sprintf\(["'](SELECT|INSERT|UPDATE|DELETE))
dialect: ere
files: *.go
tags: static
tags: quick
remediation: Build the query with a parameterised placeholder (`?` or `$1`) and pass
  values through database/sql's own argument list, never by concatenating or
  fmt.Sprintf-ing request-derived data into the query text.
references: CWE-89

id: SAST-GO-TLS_SKIP_VERIFY-01
title: TLS certificate verification disabled via InsecureSkipVerify
severity: high
confidence: high
cwe: CWE-295
owasp: A02:2021
pattern: InsecureSkipVerify[[:space:]]*:[[:space:]]*true
dialect: ere
files: *.go
tags: static
tags: quick
remediation: Never set InsecureSkipVerify to true outside a throwaway local test
  fixture. If a private CA is in play, add it to a custom tls.Config RootCAs pool
  instead of disabling verification outright.
references: CWE-295
